"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_astro_fresh.py (the fresh-cluster test: M3 and M15), for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_astro_fresh --tests tests/test_exp_astro_fresh.py --raw results/astro/fresh_raw.npz --md results/astro/fresh.md --out-env FRESH_OUT \\
        --spec tools/mutants/wp_astrofresh_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence in experiments/exp_astro_fresh.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone (planted worlds: no fresh patch is read; the
test that re-scores the stored rows with the own matcher skips in a slot because the patches are not copied). The slot's `--from-raw` report (md column) is the report regenerated from the real
raw; it is informative, not part of the criterion. The functions mutated are those of this script only: the functions it imports (`exp_astro_m2`, `exp_astro_psf`, `exp_astro_cyclefix`, `astro_fresh`, `astro_common`) are
covered by their own test files and mutation specs (the rule of `astro_fresh.py` by `wp_astrofresh_rule_own.py`).

Final run (the complete spec against the final tests file, 65 tests; the run was interrupted by a container restart after 160 mutants and the remaining 11 (M38 to M48) were run with --only in a second
slot): 171 mutants, 168 killed, 3 survivors, all equivalent on every reachable input:
  P19  `fit['kind'] != 'general'` instead of `== 'isotropic'` in patch_arrays: `fit_adequate` returns kind 'isotropic' or 'general' and nothing else, so the two tests are the same.
  T11  the second component of a `BASE_ROWS` entry (the tag source) is documentation: the code only reads the labels (`BASE_LABELS`); `baseline_dets` has the mapping written out. (The tuple is part of the code hash, which changes
       with the mutation, but a hash value is not pinned by a test: every legitimate edit would break it.)
  M48  `--freeze` writes the record twice: the second write is byte-identical to the first.
A first pass of the same spec against the first version of the tests left 33 survivors; each was killed by a test added for it (listed in the commit history of tests/test_exp_astro_fresh.py), except the three above.
"""
